>> >>>> Because it does have two (in fact, three) parses. In one, "flying"
is an adverbial adjunct (of "saw") with controlled subject; in a second, it
is "object complement" (predicate in a small-clausal complement of "saw");
in a third, it is adjunct of "plane".
>> >>>
>> >>>
>> >>> Of course, this can be a rival explanation but are those different
parses due to ambiguity of the syntactic tree?
>> >>
